prompt:
Implement a procedural terrain generation scene using Three.js (Perlin/Simplex-style noise + water surface).

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules inside <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Terrain and Noise]
(1) Use PlaneGeometry with both width and depth set to 200, and both widthSegments and heightSegments set to 128;
(2) Vertex heights must be produced by combining 2 frequency octaves (2 octaves) of Perlin- or Simplex-style noise; you must implement the noise function within the page itself (a common implementation approach may be used), and importing an external noise library is prohibited;
(3) Color vertices according to height: deep water y<0 is blue; beach 0≤y<2 is yellow; grassland 2≤y<8 is green; rock 8≤y<15 is gray; snow y≥15 is white (colors may be adjusted slightly, but the semantics must remain consistent);

[Water Surface and Atmosphere]
(4) Add a horizontal water surface: a flat, semi-transparent blue plane positioned at y=0 by default. Its actual height must be controlled by the "Water Level" parameter (consistent with the slider below);
(5) Enable fog (Fog or FogExp2) to create distance fading;

[Lighting and Controls]
(6) Use OrbitControls;
(7) The DirectionalLight must cast shadows, and the terrain (and any necessary objects) must receive/cast shadows;

[UI Controls]
(8) Provide a seed input with id="seedInput" and a "Regenerate" button with id="regenBtn" (rebuild the terrain geometry and colors based on the seed and current parameters);
(9) Provide a height scale slider with id="heightSlider", range 1–30, default 15;
(10) Provide a water level slider with id="waterSlider", range -5–10, default 0 (the water surface's world-coordinate y must match this value, and the HUD display must stay synchronized);

[HUD]
(11) Display in real time: vertex count with id="vertexCount", maximum height with id="maxHeight", minimum height with id="minHeight", and current water level with id="waterLevel" (consistent with __3D_STATE__.waterLevel);

[State Exposure (Required)]
(12) Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame. It must contain at least: vertexCount (the terrain mesh vertex count, as an integer), maxHeight, minHeight, waterLevel (the current water level, consistent with the slider), heightScale (the current height scaling factor), seed (either a string or number is acceptable, but it must remain synchronized with the input), and terrainCenter:{x,y,z} (the world coordinates of the terrain geometry's center).

Output a single HTML file that can be opened directly through a local HTTP server.
